nothing says summer like watermelon but  when it comes to cocktails watermelon is  a very challenging ingredient to work  with because there's so much watering  and already if you add ice essentially  more water it dilutes it stretches it  out and you lose that trademark  watermelon flavor but there are ways  around it and I'm going to show you a  cocktail  the retains all of watermelons thirst  quenching glory it is called the  watermelon spritz what you're going to  need for this cocktail is some fresh  watermelon juice a light bitter Italian  liqueur a little bit of vodka and some  Rose a champagne so we're going to build  this drink right in the glass there's no  shaking or stirring because that would  dilute it and we lose that watermelon  flavor the key to a great watermelon  drink is using watermelon juice which  you can get in a number of ways you  could just muddle some in a glass or  container until it's pretty much all  water or you can run us through a juicer  which is the easiest you can also put it  in a blender or a food processor just  blend it right up and strain out the  solids so we're going to have two ounces  of watermelon juice and add it right  into the glass now I can add two ounces  of my bitter aperitif go for something  on the lighter side as bitters are very  concentrated you'll need a few dashes  but bitter liqueurs are very popular in  Italy and France and they are drank all  by themselves in Italy they're called  Amaro's and France they're called at  mayors  both of them just mean bitter so two  ounces of the bitter liqueur it's on the  lighter side so two ounces really isn't  that much alcohol  now half an ounce of vodka just to bump  up the booze a little bit and give it an  extra kick you could use 3/4 full ounce  of vodka if you want it now we're gonna  throw in our ice and now we're going to  add our rose a champagne you can easily  make this drink for a group of people  like putting this all in a pitcher just  add the champagne last because you want  those bubbles to be nice and fresh top  it off about 3 ounces so wow that looks  amazing and finally we're going to  garnish this with a few cucumber slices  and some strawberries surprisingly the  combination of two cumber and strawberry  kind of boosts that watermelon flavor  it just incorporate it a little bit of a  stir and that is the watermelon spritz  perfect for sitting by the pool or in a  cafe on the streets of Italy or just  about anywhere at all if you like that  drink subscribe to the GQ channel for  more
 

